# requirements-kokoro.in : the narrator's environment (voice.py engine kokoro-ts), a side Python 3.13 environment,
# because kokoro-onnx 0.6.1 declares requires-python <3.14; engine/requirements.txt stays Pillow and numpy only. These
# lines are the one place the pins live; voice.py runs the compiled lock. After a change, compile the lock again from
# this folder:
#   uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.13 requirements-kokoro.in -o requirements-kokoro.txt
# voice.py hashes requirements-kokoro.txt into every part's cache key, so a new lock synthesizes again. envs.py builds
# the environment from the lock with uv pip install --require-hashes, so a wheel whose sha256 differs from the lock's
# is refused. NOT installed by setup.sh. Model and voice files are separate downloads (sizes,
# hashes and licences in voice.py KOKORO_FILES and references/voice.md), never fetched without the user's yes.
# Every package that changes the phonemes or the sound is pinned here (espeak-ng comes in espeakng-loader). Licences:
# kokoro-onnx MIT, onnxruntime MIT, phonemizer GPL-3.0, espeakng-loader bundles espeak-ng (GPL-3.0). Versions read from
# PyPI on 2026-10-28, 2026-11-03 and 2026-11-16 (onnxruntime 1.32.0, phonemizer 3.6.0, numpy 2.5.5).
kokoro-onnx==0.6.1
onnxruntime==1.32.0
phonemizer==3.6.0
espeakng-loader==0.2.4
numpy==2.5.5
